# Build-context allowlist for the API image.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's
# `.dockerignore`, so this file governs the API build alone. The root `.dockerignore`
# still governs the web image, whose needs are the exact opposite of this one's.
#
# The API build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the runtime needs
# `packages/brand/assets` and a context of `services/commerce-api` can never reach it.
# Widening the context is what made the media 404 possible to fix; it is also what makes
# it possible to ship `.git`, `.env` and the immutable Side A handoff by accident. So this
# is written as DENY EVERYTHING, then allow the handful of paths the runtime actually
# needs — an allowlist, matching the media route's own allow-list posture.
#
# Adding a file to the image therefore requires an explicit line here. That is the point.
# The image contents are verified against this intent by
# `scripts/validation/container_media_acceptance.py`, which inspects the built artifact
# rather than trusting this file to be right.

# ---- deny everything -----------------------------------------------------------------
**

# ---- allow: the service's runtime source and data ------------------------------------
!services/commerce-api/requirements.txt
!services/commerce-api/alembic.ini
!services/commerce-api/manage.py
!services/commerce-api/notification_worker.py
!services/commerce-api/docker-entrypoint.sh
!services/commerce-api/app
!services/commerce-api/app/**
!services/commerce-api/data
!services/commerce-api/data/**
!services/commerce-api/migrations
!services/commerce-api/migrations/**

# ---- allow: the normalized brand package, and ONLY its assets and manifests -----------
# The immutable Side A handoff under handoffs/incoming/ is NOT here and must never be.
# Runtime serves the generated package; the handoff is checksum-protected evidence.
!packages/brand/assets
!packages/brand/assets/**
!packages/brand/assets.json
!packages/brand/product-media.json

# ---- allow: the asset verifier that makes the build fail on a missing asset -----------
!scripts/brand/verify_packaged_assets.py

# ---- re-deny things that could otherwise ride in on the allowances above --------------
# Order matters: these come last, so they win over the `!` lines.
services/commerce-api/tests
services/commerce-api/tests/**
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-wal
**/*.sqlite3-shm
**/.env
**/.env.*
